text:
Since today grief pours night across the whole circle of pure light, and the sun, dimmed in dark shadow, gives tears to fire and voice to wind;


since death's black confinement reveals the grave with trembling, and the mountain obstructing the nearby sea's plain splits attentively;


your heart is hard stone, diamond, if so severe a death does not drown your face through your eyes.


Yet it is not stone, for if it were, pity at seeing loving God would have broken it among the other stones.
